jank-26: native numerics without hints: a native loop local stays native only while recur keeps it
native, else it is boxed (Clojure's auto-boxed loop arg)
(cohost doc/upstream/jank-26-native-inference.md; lane U6, order U6-2)

Base: jank-lang/jank f3d82d65499920f81216e9235bd5d3a34a968e3f with the series before it in
upstream/jank/patches/series (11, 13, 14, 12-21, 18, 19, 15a-16, 15b-17, 22, 20). Apply from the
clone's root: git apply <this file>.

What the base already infers without hints (12-21 and 20; nothing here changes it): a loop or let
local initialized from an integer or real literal is native (i64 / f64); a let local from a native
expression is native; an if whose branches are native (or one branch recurs) keeps the native type;
+ - * / inc dec on native operands stay native and checked; a fn with untyped params gets native
loops inside it.

Merge note (coordinator, 2026-11-02 3:00 PM ET): var::deref_inline and the generated deref_inline call
(var.hpp, cpp_processor.cpp) were implemented identically by 24-direct-calls, which precedes this
patch in the series; those two hunks are dropped here and 24 carries them. This patch is the
loop-widening change (3 files).

Files:
- compiler+runtime/src/cpp/jank/analyze/processor.cpp, include .../analyze/expr/let.hpp,
  .../analyze/processor.hpp: a native loop binding stays native only while every recur argument
  for it is a native number of the same kind (integer for an integer, real for a real). Otherwise
  analyze_recur flags the binding (expr::let::loop_box_bindings) and analyze_loop analyzes the
  loop again with the flagged bindings boxed (Clojure's auto-boxed loop arg); each round boxes at
  least one more binding, so it ends. Before, the argument was converted into the native type: a
  real truncated into an integer local ((loop [s 0] ... (recur (+ s 1.5))) gave 3 for 4.5), an
  object unboxed with a throw ("An object of type integer was expected here, but a small_real was
  provided"), and (recur nil) or a string failed to compile (from_object ambiguous).
- (not in this patch: var::deref_inline and the generated deref_inline call are 24-direct-calls';
  see the merge note above. The P2/H0 call rows below were measured with them.)

